description:
Mouse wheel scroll in `thc window` (GPU terminal) is backwards — scrolling wheel up moves the view down and vice versa.

## Root Cause

In `crates/thermal-conductor/src/window.rs` lines 2758-2761, the scroll direction mapping is inverted:

```rust
if vertical.discrete > 0 {
    t.scroll_display(Scroll::Delta(3));    // positive discrete = wheel down, but Delta(3) scrolls DOWN into history
} else if vertical.discrete < 0 {
    t.scroll_display(Scroll::Delta(-3));   // negative discrete = wheel up, but Delta(-3) scrolls UP (toward newer)
}
```

In smithay-client-toolkit's pointer axis events, `vertical.discrete > 0` means **wheel scrolled down** (away from user). `Scroll::Delta(positive)` in alacritty_terminal means **scroll down into history** (view moves up). So wheel-down currently scrolls into history, but the natural expectation is: wheel-up = scroll back into history, wheel-down = scroll toward present.

## Fix

Swap the delta signs:

```rust
if vertical.discrete > 0 {
    t.scroll_display(Scroll::Delta(-3));   // wheel down → scroll toward present
} else if vertical.discrete < 0 {
    t.scroll_display(Scroll::Delta(3));    // wheel up → scroll into history
}
```

## Key Files
- `crates/thermal-conductor/src/window.rs:2758` — the two lines to swap

