## Context
When scrolled into scrollback history, the cursor disappears or renders at a garbage position. `cursor.point.line.0` is negative (Line is i32) during scrollback, and casting to usize wraps to a huge value.

## Task
Fix cursor row handling in `grid_renderer.rs` at ~line 3173 and ~3297. Before casting Line to usize, check if the value is negative. If negative, skip cursor rendering (cursor is off-screen above the viewport during scrollback).

```rust
// Guard against negative line values during scrollback
let cursor_row = cursor.point.line.0;
if cursor_row < 0 {
    // Cursor is in scrollback above viewport — don't render
    return; // or continue, depending on context
}
let row = cursor_row as usize;
```

Also check any other `line.0 as usize` casts in the cursor rendering path.

